  "bodyTypst": "The Maclaurin series for the function $f$ is given by\n\n$ f(x)= sum_(n = 0)^(oo) frac((2 x)^(n + 1),n + 1)= 2 x + frac(4 x^(2),2)+ frac(8 x^(3),3)+ frac(16 x^(4),4)+ dots.h.c + frac((2 x)^(n + 1),n + 1)+ dots.h.c $\n\non its interval of convergence.\n\n(a) Find the interval of convergence of the Maclaurin series for $f$. Justify your answer.\n\n(b) Find the first four terms and the general term for the Maclaurin series for $f'(x)$.\n\n(c) Use the Maclaurin series you found in part (b) to find the value of $f'lr((- frac(1,3)))$.",
